<Concept title="Technique progression integrity" section="States">
<p>Completes integration portions of #343/#747 and eligibility in #745. Existing
class resource caps, character-level disk gates, power and PP formulas remain
remake tuning; this work does not claim original stat/formula parity.</p>
<ul>
<li>New shop/drop disks MUST belong to the basic tier, matching /mechanics/techs.
Advanced catalogue entries without a learnable base (including Grants/Megid)
MUST NOT be sold or dropped as invisible progression dead ends.</li>
<li>Disk levels MUST be positive and no greater than 30. New disks MUST also fit
the highest supported class cap for their group (currently 15); difficulty and
boss/rare bonuses MUST NOT mint disks that no class can learn. Class/group caps and
character-level requirements MUST apply before consumption. Duplicate or lower
levels MUST fail without consuming an inventory copy.</li>
<li>Old saved advanced learned entries MAY remain usable for compatibility, but
MUST obey class/group caps. A charged variant MUST use at least its learned base
level, even when an older variant entry is present. CASTs and unknown classes
MUST resolve level zero, including stale imported saves and palette entries.</li>
<li>Successful disk use MUST consume only the selected copy. Save/reload MUST
preserve the upgrade and consumed inventory. Power and PP cost MUST use the same
resolved level as projectile status level.</li>
<li>A charge MUST NOT start for an unlearned/class-forbidden technique or while
already attacking/dodging. Direct cast requests while hurt, down or defeated
MUST NOT spend PP. Existing immediate release timing is retained; event-frame
release and full Force balance/pacing remain open for #745/#747.</li>
</ul>
<p>Tests: technique_progression_tests.gd and technique_progression_probe.tscn.
The live probe uses a fresh FOmar, earned EXP to reach a disk gate, inventory
learning, real Barta projectiles, PP spending, and a persisted reload.</p>
</Concept>
